<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Android Auto Backup rules for API 31 and above.
    Below API 31 the platform ignores this file and reads backup_rules.xml
    instead, so the two files must keep the same exclusions.

    QuisquisLingo has no server, so a device backup is the only way a learner
    keeps progress across a phone change. Learner profiles, progress, XP,
    streaks, Review history, local course edits, settings and the Access PIN
    verifier are therefore backed up deliberately. The Access PIN is a casual
    access guard for a shared family device, not a security boundary.

    Only bulk media is excluded, and the reason is the 25 MB Auto Backup quota,
    not privacy: a single Image Bank import can reach 50 MB on its own, and an
    app that exceeds the quota has its backup silently disabled entirely. Losing
    progress that way would be far worse than re-importing media.

    These three folders live under getApplicationSupportDirectory(), which is
    getFilesDir() on Android, so they belong to domain="file". They are the same
    folders AppResetService treats as bulk media (_imageFolders, _audioFolders).
    Media is re-importable from the user's own files; progress is not.

    device-transfer is deliberately omitted so that a direct phone-to-phone
    transfer, which has no such quota, still carries the media across.
-->
<data-extraction-rules>
    <cloud-backup>
        <exclude domain="file" path="image_banks/" />
        <exclude domain="file" path="exercise_images/" />
        <exclude domain="file" path="quisquislingo_audio/" />
    </cloud-backup>
</data-extraction-rules>
